  (text "SAO++ power select: the switch common feeds the LEDs. Position 1 = badge 3.3 V, position 2 = OFF (pin 2 unconnected), position 3 = coin cell." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 38.1 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "eacc80a3-76fb-58e5-a658-cbd9868bb25b"))
  (text "The badge supply and the coin cell sit on separate switch contacts and are never connected to each other." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 41.910000000000004 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "97569c56-ca6b-5923-aec9-f73ef2fed445"))
  (text "LED-only board: SDA, SCL, GPIO1 and GPIO2 are not connected (as on the original), so no series diode is needed on the cell (docs/standard.md section 3)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 45.72 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "5a943a57-14b4-5404-a0c5-74e47eba494b"))
  (text "D1, D2: white reverse-mount LEDs on the back, shining through the board where NorthSec's two 3 mm through-hole LEDs stood." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 124.46 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9af11dd2-408f-50d2-8394-56b66b7e902a"))
  (text "One 1.3k resistor per LED (the original used 330 ohm on 3.3 V): about 0.45 mA each on badge power, about 0.2 mA each on a fresh cell." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 128.26999999999998 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "bab96877-d602-5c46-a820-040611a3778e"))
